# Diamond-structure silicon, conventional cubic cell (8 atoms).
# Written in space group P1 on purpose: every atom is listed explicitly,
# so no symmetry expansion is needed and every reader (ASE, pymatgen,
# VESTA, Open Babel) produces exactly the same 8 atoms.
# Lattice parameter a = 5.431 A (room-temperature experiment; the CODATA
# recommended lattice parameter of Si is 5.431020511 A).
# Run check_symmetry.py to let spglib recover Fd-3m (No. 227).
data_Si_diamond_P1
_chemical_name_common             'silicon, diamond structure'
_chemical_formula_sum             'Si8'
_cell_length_a                    5.431000
_cell_length_b                    5.431000
_cell_length_c                    5.431000
_cell_angle_alpha                 90.000000
_cell_angle_beta                  90.000000
_cell_angle_gamma                 90.000000
_cell_volume                      160.1924
_cell_formula_units_Z             8
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M    'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number       1
loop_
_symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz
  'x, y, z'
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
_atom_site_occupancy
Si1  Si  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000  1.0
Si2  Si  0.000000  0.500000  0.500000  1.0
Si3  Si  0.500000  0.000000  0.500000  1.0
Si4  Si  0.500000  0.500000  0.000000  1.0
Si5  Si  0.250000  0.250000  0.250000  1.0
Si6  Si  0.250000  0.750000  0.750000  1.0
Si7  Si  0.750000  0.250000  0.750000  1.0
Si8  Si  0.750000  0.750000  0.250000  1.0
